This Python game loop is nondeterministic because it integrates with the raw frame delta instead of a fixed step:

class Sim:
    def __init__(self):
        self.x = 0.0
        self.v = 3.0
    def update(self, frame_dt):
        self.x += self.v * frame_dt

def run(frames):
    s = Sim()
    for dt in frames:
        s.update(dt)
    return s.x

Two players with different frame pacing diverge. Put this in `sim.py`, first write a pytest test proving that frames [0.016]*125 and [0.032]*62+[0.016] (same total time within one step) yield different trajectories when you sample x at fixed sim-times, then refactor to a fixed 1/50s timestep with an accumulator so sampled states become identical, keeping the failing-then-passing test history. Show pytest passing.

